From: dresden196 <50474030+dresden196@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] NickelOS: Linux apps may lock the pointer

Exo grants pointer lock (zwp_pointer_constraints_v1) only where the
window's security delegate allows it, and ChromeSecurityDelegate, which
NickelOS's Linux apps get, allows it for ARC windows only. Xwayland locks
the pointer to carry out X11 games' pointer warps (mouse look re-centres
the pointer every frame) and takes relative motion while it is locked;
refused, the real pointer went on to the screen's edge: in Left 4 Dead 2 a
turn stopped short (Dresden also noticed the view lagging).

Linux apps lock it as on a Linux desktop. Exo's own limits stay: only the
active window, ended when the focus moves, back with the focus.

diff --git a/chrome/browser/ash/exo/chrome_security_delegate.cc b/chrome/browser/ash/exo/chrome_security_delegate.cc
index 02ffe6b5d0ab7..5a24e51596b3b 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/ash/exo/chrome_security_delegate.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/ash/exo/chrome_security_delegate.cc
@@ -360,7 +360,14 @@ bool ChromeSecurityDelegate::CanSelfActivate(aura::Window* window) const {
 bool ChromeSecurityDelegate::CanLockPointer(aura::Window* window) const {
   // TODO(b/200896773): Move this out from exo's default security delegate
   // define in client's security delegates.
-  return ash::IsArcWindow(window);
+  // NickelOS: this server's other clients are the user's Linux apps on the
+  // device (VMs have their own delegates), which lock the pointer as on a
+  // Linux desktop: games, and Xwayland for X11 games, whose mouse look
+  // warps the pointer (refused, the turn stopped at the screen's edge). Exo
+  // still grants it only to the active window, ends it when the focus
+  // moves (Alt+Tab, the launcher, Overview) and gives it back when the
+  // window has the focus again.
+  return true;
 }
 
 ChromeSecurityDelegate::SetBoundsPolicy ChromeSecurityDelegate::CanSetBounds(
